'''''Hypericum montanum''''' is a plant species in the genus ''[[Hypericum]]'' commonly known as '''pale St. John's-wort''' or '''mountain St. John's wort'''.<ref>[https://www.rhs.org.uk/Plants/9014/Pale-St-John-s-wort/Details Royal Horticultural Society]</ref> It is native to Eurasia and [[Morocco]] in North Africa.<ref name=grin>{{GRIN | access-date = 19 January 2018}}</ref>

==Description==
''Hypericum montanum'' are normally from 20 to 80 centimeters (8–32 inches). Its flower has five petals and it flowers from July to August.<ref>[http://www.luontoportti.com/suomi/en/kukkakasvit/mountain-st-johns-wort Nature Gate: Luontoportti]</ref>

